### Using Jsoup Library to Parse HTML and Extract Data

Jsoup is a Java library that allows you to parse HTML and extract data in a flexible and easy-to-use way. Here's an example of how you could use it to parse a simple HTML page and extract the text content of each table row:

```java
import org.jsoup.Jsoup;
import org.jsoup.nodes.Document;
import org.jsoup.select.Elements;

public class JsoupParser {

    public static void main(String[] args) {
        String html = "<html><body><table id='example'><tr><td>John</td></tr><tr><td>Doe</td></tr></table></body></html>";
        Document document = Jsoup.parse(html);
        Elements tableRows = document.select("table tr");
        
        for (Elements rows : tableRows) {
            System.out.println(rows.text());
        }
    }
}
```

### Using Jsoup Library to Parse HTML and Extract Data with a More Complex Structure

If your HTML page has a more complex structure, you may need to use the `select()` method in combination with other methods like `text()`, `trim()`, and `replace()` to extract the data. Here's an example of how you could do this:

```java
import org.jsoup.Jsoup;
import org.jsoup.nodes.Document;
import org.jsoup.select.Elements;

public class JsoupParser {

    public static void main(String[] args) {
        String html = "<html><body><table id='example'><tr><td>John</td></tr><tr><td>Doe</td></tr><tr><td>Jane</td></tr></table></body></html>";
        Document document = Jsoup.parse(html);
        
        Elements tableRows = document.select("table tr");
        for (Elements rows : tableRows) {
            System.out.println(rows.text());
            
            // Get the first and last cells in each row
            Elements firstCell = rows.select("td:first-child").first();
            Elements lastCell = rows.select("td:last-child").last();
            
            // Print the contents of these cells
            System.out.println(firstCell.text() + " - " + lastCell.text());
        }
    }
}
```

